w: 5.~Love caused Thine in- car- na- tion Love brought Thee down to me; 
w: 6.~Re- joice, then, ye sad\-- hear- ted, Who sit in deep- est gloom,
w: 7.~No care nor ef- fort ei- ther Is nee- ded day or night,
w: 8.~Sin's debt, that fear- ful bur- den, Let not your souls dis- tress;
w: 9.~Why should the wi- cked move you? Heed not their craft and spite!
w: 10.~He comes to judge the na- tions, A ter- ror to His foes,
